---
/**
 * /news/premium-lock-for-auto
 *
 * The first post of the small content engine. Written ONLY from the facts the
 * client supplied: the Eventual Climate launch email (2026-10-21) and the
 * Eventual Climate blog post "Premium Lock for Auto is Here!" (2026-10-21).
 * No invented numbers, no copied partner prose.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FaqBlock from '../../components/FaqBlock.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../config/site.js';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../../lib/schema.js';

const path = '/news/premium-lock-for-auto';
const trail = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Premium Lock', path: '/specialty/premium-lock' },
  { name: 'Premium Lock for Auto', path },
];

const articleFaq = [
  {
    q: 'Is Premium Lock for Auto available in Missouri and Kansas?',
    a: 'Yes. It is available in all 50 states with any admitted lines carrier, on 6- or 12-month policies. We check eligibility against your actual policy before recommending it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does this replace my normal renewal review?',
    a: 'No. We still review your policies every year, because your life changes even when the price is locked. What Premium Lock addresses is the carrier-initiated increase at renewal, so the number you budgeted is the number you get.',
  },
];

const schema = [
  webPageSchema({
    path,
    title: 'Premium Lock for Auto is here',
    description:
      'Premium Lock for Auto extends 3 years of pricing predictability from homes to cars, available in all 50 states with any admitted lines carrier.',
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(trail),
  faqSchema({ faqs: articleFaq, path }),
  {
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Premium Lock for Auto is here',
    datePublished: '2026-10-21',
    author: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
    publisher: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` },
    inLanguage: 'en-US',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Premium Lock for Auto | 3-Year Price Predictability | BIG"
  description="Premium Lock for Auto extends 3 years of pricing predictability from homes to cars, available in all 50 states on 6 or 12 month policies."
  path={path}
  schema={schema}
>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={trail} />

  <article class="container-page py-12">
    <header class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-brand-700)]">
        October 21, 2026 · Two minute read
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Premium Lock for Auto is here</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
        By Ballentine Insurance Group, a Farmers agency serving Lee's Summit and
        the Kansas City Northland.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink-soft)]">
        Eventual Climate launched Premium Lock for Auto on October 21, 2026,
        extending the multi-year pricing guarantee from homes to cars. Here is
        what that means for Kansas City drivers.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-page mt-10 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>What changed</h2>
      <p>
        Premium Lock started with homeowners, and the people who used it asked
        for the same predictability on the other big recurring bill: the car.
        The answer arrived this week. Premium Lock for Auto is live, available
        in all 50 states with any admitted lines carrier, on 6- or 12-month
        policies, creating 3 years of pricing predictability.
      </p>

      <h2>Why it matters now</h2>
      <p>
        The average American already pays more to insure their car than their
        home, which makes auto an overlooked but significant financial stress.
        Home insurance is often hidden inside the mortgage escrow payment;
        auto is the visible, frequent bill that gets re-shopped and serviced
        every term. That is exactly where renewal surprises hurt most.
      </p>
      <p>
        As Dylan DiMarchi, Eventual&rsquo;s CEO, put it at launch: &ldquo;The
        multi-year nature of Premium Lock handily resolves most auto retention
        problems for our distribution partners.&rdquo; For you, that means
        price-sensitive drivers get clarity on their future expenses instead
        of a surprise at renewal.
      </p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        Quotes come through the Premium Lock portal. You drag and drop a
        declarations page into the portal&rsquo;s AI chat window, and the
        quote builds itself with no manual entry. Before anything is quoted,
        we check eligibility against your actual policy and confirm the exact
        terms in writing, because a rate promise with unstated exceptions is
        worse than no promise at all.
      </p>

      <h2>What Premium Lock is not</h2>
      <p>
        No product locks a rate forever. Taxes, fees, and changes you make to
        the policy can still move the premium. What Premium Lock addresses is
        the carrier-initiated increase at renewal, so the number you budgeted
        is the number you get.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions we have been asked</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl">
      <FaqBlock faqs={articleFaq} />
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <a href="/specialty/premium-lock" class="btn btn-primary">How Premium Lock works</a>
      <a href="/get-a-quote?coverage=auto" class="btn btn-secondary">Start an auto quote</a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
